Starting with Beth being 18 and her sister 5, we note a 13-year age difference. For Beth to be twice her sister's age, her sister must be 18/2 = 9 years old. Since Beth's sister is currently 5, she needs to age by 9 - 5 = 4 years to meet this criteria. So, in 4 years, Beth will be twice her sister's age.
\boxed{4}
Answer: 4


